@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam ClassBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #ffffff

title The provider and facility record as stored, and the two projections taken from it: the five things a row carries and everything the detail carries

class "Provider (stored)" as Stored #ffffff {
  .. registry facts ..
  npi
  entity_type_code
  provider_first_name / middle / last_name_legal_name
  provider_name_prefix_text / suffix / credential_text
  provider_organization_name_legal_business_name
  provider_other_organization_name (+ type code)
  is_organization_subpart, parent_organization_lbn
  provider_enumeration_date
  practice_addresses[], business_address
  taxonomies[] { code, primary }
  other_identifiers[]
  authorized_official_* (organizations only)
  .. normalised from registry ..
  licenses[] { state, number }
  insurance[] { insurance_type, payer_name, state, payer_id }
  active[] { is_active, ... } appended on change
  .. ours, not the registry's ..
  <b>address.county</b> { name, fips, rucc, <b>urban</b>, source }
  <b>address.lat / lng</b>
  <b>address.state_label / country_code_label</b>
  <b>can_prescribe / is_homeopathic / is_disqualified</b>
  <b>facility_type_descriptions[]</b> { classification, specialization, definition }
  <b>primary_taxonomy_code</b>
  <b>bad_data / out_of_scope</b>
  <b>embedding / embedding_model / embedding_version</b>
  <b>load_id / loaded_at / chunk_id / row_index_in_chunk</b>
  <b>provenance</b> { origin, last_touched_at, real_time_sync_count }
}

note right of Stored
  The bold fields are the pipeline's and the geocoder's.
  NPPES has never heard of any of them, which is why the
  detail sync compares only the fields the registry owns
  and starts a write-back from our address rather than
  from the live one.
end note

class "Result row — care giver" as Row #f3f4f6 {
  name
  npi
  taxonomy_code
  matched_specialty_code / matched_specialty_label
  taxonomy_codes[]
  address (one line, the matched practice address)
  phone
  <b>county</b> (the name only, no urban standing)
  <b>lat / lng</b>
}

class "Result row — facility" as FRow #f3f4f6 {
  facility (legal business name)
  practice_address_count
  primary_practice_address
  facility_type (primary taxonomy, resolved server-side)
  npi
}

note bottom of FRow
  Fixed at five things by requirement, and the projection
  is where that is enforced rather than the renderer: a
  renderer sent a sixth field is one edit from painting it.
end note

class "ProviderDetailOutput" as Detail #ffffff {
  provider_name, npi
  entity_type ("1" care giver, "2" facility)
  unresolved_licensing_state
}

class Identity {
  name_prefix, first, middle, last
  credentials
  primary_taxonomy_display
  status_active
  enumeration_date
}
class OrganizationIdentity {
  legal_business_name
  other_organization_name (+ kind, as a label)
  enumeration_date, status_active
  is_subpart, parent_organization_name
}
class Address {
  address_type, line1, line2
  city, state, zip, country, phone
}
class County {
  <b>name</b>
  <b>urban</b> (absent when unknown)
}
class License {
  state, number
}
class Insurance {
  coverage_kind, issuer, state, identifier
}
class Taxonomy {
  code, display_name, primary
}
class AuthorizedOfficial {
  last, first, middle
  title_or_position, credential
}
class FacilityKind {
  code, classification
  specialization, definition
}
class ResearchSite {
  url, name, guidance
}

Stored ..> Row : projected for a care-giver list
Stored ..> FRow : projected for a facility list
Stored ..> Detail : projected for one open record

Detail *-- Identity
Detail *-- OrganizationIdentity
Detail *-- Address
Address *-- County
Detail *-- License
Detail *-- Insurance
Detail *-- Taxonomy
Detail *-- AuthorizedOfficial
Detail *-- FacilityKind
Detail *-- ResearchSite

note right of Detail
  A row carries what a list can be read from; everything
  else waits for the detail. The three organization blocks
  are present on a facility and absent on a care giver, so
  the renderer selects on entity_type rather than on the
  shape of the data.

  Two things the record holds are deliberately absent here:
  the employer identification number and the parent
  organization's taxpayer identification number. The
  projection not naming them is the enforcement.
end note

note bottom of County
  Urban standing is the pipeline's RUCC pass, not a
  registry fact. It is absent rather than defaulted on an
  address the pipeline has not yet reached — a brand-new
  address written back from a live registry answer has a
  county name from the geocoder and no urban standing.
end note

@enduml
